---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="Developer API Docs - SuperAda" description="Public SuperAda API documentation with authentication notes, endpoints, and example requests for agents and developers." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="docs-shell" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
			<section class="docs-hero">
				<div class="kicker">Developer docs</div>
				<h1 id="docs-title">SuperAda public API and agent docs.</h1>
				<p class="lede">Use this page as the human-readable companion to <a href="/openapi.json">/openapi.json</a>. It documents authentication, versioned public endpoints, request shapes, response formats, deprecation signals, and examples so agents can discover the API from the homepage without guessing.</p>
				<div class="docs-actions" aria-label="Developer resources">
					<a class="pill-link" href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI JSON</a>
					<a class="pill-link" href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
					<a class="pill-link" href="/sitemap-index.xml">Sitemap</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="docs-grid" aria-label="API overview">
				<article class="docs-card">
					<h2>Base URL</h2>
					<p>All public endpoints are served from the canonical site origin.</p>
					<pre><code>https://superada.ai</code></pre>
				</article>

				<article class="docs-card">
					<h2>Authentication</h2>
					<p>Current public API endpoints do not require an API key from clients. Write-style endpoints are protected by CORS, request validation, server-side storage credentials, and per-IP rate limits. Do not send secrets in request bodies.</p>
				</article>

				<article class="docs-card">
					<h2>Error format</h2>
					<p>API errors are machine-parseable JSON with a stable code, human message, and resolution hint.</p>
					<pre><code>{`{
  "ok": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "method_not_allowed",
    "message": "POST only.",
    "hint": "Send a POST request with a JSON body; see /openapi.json."
  }
}`}</code></pre>
				</article>
			</section>

			<section class="docs-panel" aria-labelledby="versioning-policy">
				<h2 id="versioning-policy">REST versioning and deprecation policy</h2>
				<p>The current public API is <strong>version 1</strong>. Agents should integrate against the canonical versioned paths under <code>/api/v1/...</code>, such as <code>/api/v1/benchmarks</code> and <code>/api/v1/subscribe</code>. The older unprefixed <code>/api/...</code> paths remain compatibility aliases for v1.</p>
				<p>Breaking API changes will ship in a new major versioned namespace, for example <code>/api/v2/subscribe</code>. Non-breaking additions, such as optional response fields or new static benchmark datasets, may be added to v1 without changing existing fields.</p>
				<p>Active v1 responses include <code>API-Version: 1</code>, <code>X-API-Version: 1</code>, and <code>Deprecation: false</code>. If an endpoint becomes deprecated, SuperAda will change that signal to <code>Deprecation: true</code>, include a <code>Sunset</code> header with the planned retirement date, keep a policy <code>Link</code> header, and list the replacement path on this page.</p>
				<p>SuperAda aims to provide at least 90 days of notice before removing a public API endpoint unless security, abuse, or legal requirements force a faster shutdown.</p>
				<pre><code>{`API-Version: 1
X-API-Version: 1
Deprecation: false
Link: <https://superada.ai/developers/#versioning-policy>; rel="deprecation"; type="text/html"

# Future deprecated endpoint example:
Deprecation: true
Sunset: Wed, 31 Dec 2027 23:59:59 GMT`}</code></pre>
			</section>

			<section class="docs-panel" aria-labelledby="rate-limits-title">
				<h2 id="rate-limits-title">Rate limits</h2>
				<p>API responses include standard rate-limit headers so agents can self-throttle instead of retrying blindly. Serverless write endpoints currently allow 5 requests per 60-second window per client IP. Static public JSON endpoints publish a read-policy header for discovery and cache-aware clients.</p>
				<pre><code>{`RateLimit-Limit: 5
RateLimit-Remaining: 4
RateLimit-Reset: 60
RateLimit-Policy: 5;w=60`}</code></pre>
				<p>When a client exceeds a write-endpoint limit, the API returns <code>429</code> with <code>Retry-After</code> plus the structured JSON error format documented above.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="docs-panel" aria-labelledby="endpoints-title">
				<h2 id="endpoints-title">Endpoints</h2>
				<div class="endpoint-list">
					<article>
						<h3><code>GET /openapi.json</code></h3>
						<p>Machine-readable OpenAPI 3.1 description of the supported SuperAda API surface.</p>
						<pre><code>curl -sS https://superada.ai/openapi.json</code></pre>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3><code>GET /llms.txt</code></h3>
						<p>Agent-readable site orientation: what SuperAda is, when to use the site, key links, and API discovery pointers.</p>
						<pre><code>curl -sS https://superada.ai/llms.txt</code></pre>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3><code>POST /api/v1/subscribe</code></h3>
						<p>Subscribe a human or agent to SuperAda updates. Requires JSON. Rate limited to reduce abuse. <code>/api/subscribe</code> remains a v1 compatibility alias.</p>
						<pre><code>{`curl -sS https://superada.ai/api/v1/subscribe \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "subscriberType": "agent",
    "agentName": "Example Watcher",
    "topics": ["ship-log", "releases"]
  }'`}</code></pre>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3><code>POST /api/v1/workshop-feedback</code></h3>
						<p>Submit feedback for a SuperAda workshop. Requires ratings from 1 to 5 and at least one useful text field. <code>/api/workshop-feedback</code> remains a v1 compatibility alias.</p>
						<pre><code>{`curl -sS https://superada.ai/api/v1/workshop-feedback \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "ratings": {
      "overall": 5,
      "clarity": 5,
      "pace": 4,
      "handsOn": 5,
      "usefulness": 5
    },
    "biggestTakeaway": "Agents need operational proof, not autonomy theatre."
  }'`}</code></pre>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3><code>GET /api/v1/benchmarks</code> and benchmark JSON endpoints</h3>
						<p>Static benchmark data used by the site, including model, browser, memory, workload-readiness, and audio catalog data. See <a href="/openapi.json">/openapi.json</a> for the full versioned list. <code>/api/benchmarks</code> remains a v1 compatibility alias.</p>
						<pre><code>curl -sS https://superada.ai/api/v1/benchmarks</code></pre>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="docs-panel" aria-labelledby="negotiation-title">
				<h2 id="negotiation-title">Content negotiation</h2>
				<p>The homepage supports Markdown negotiation for agents. Send <code>Accept: text/markdown</code> to receive Markdown, or <code>Accept: text/html</code> for the normal webpage. Responses include <code>Vary: Accept</code> where content differs by request header.</p>
				<pre><code>curl -sS -H 'Accept: text/markdown' https://superada.ai/</code></pre>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.docs-shell { width: min(100%, 1120px); margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(54px, 7vw, 96px) 32px 90px; }
	.docs-hero { margin-bottom: 28px; }
	.docs-hero h1 { max-width: 900px; font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.055em; }
	.docs-hero .lede { max-width: 820px; }
	.docs-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 24px; }
	.pill-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 42px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--panel); font-weight: 800; }
	.docs-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin-top: 30px; }
	.docs-card, .docs-panel { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 26px; background: linear-gradient(145deg, var(--panel), color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel-soft) 68%, transparent)); box-shadow: 0 16px 48px color-mix(in srgb, var(--glow) 16%, transparent); }
	.docs-card { padding: 24px; }
	.docs-panel { margin-top: 16px; padding: 30px; }
	.docs-card h2, .docs-panel h2 { font-size: 26px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
	.docs-card p, .docs-panel p, .endpoint-list p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.72; }
	.endpoint-list { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
	.endpoint-list article { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 18px; }
	.endpoint-list article:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
	.endpoint-list h3 { font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
	pre { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 14px; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 82%, black); color: var(--text); }
	code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', monospace; font-size: .9em; }
	p code, h3 code { color: var(--text); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 7px; padding: 1px 5px; }
	@media (max-width: 860px) { .docs-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
